MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_001: No, no, it's clear enough your mind's made up.\nJust leave.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_002: You overheard that? Well, we weren't talking about\nanything important, but... Agh!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_003: Alright, if you must pry! That man is a writer and\none of my closest friends.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_004: His cold countenance would light up with passion\nwhenever we discussed literature.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_005: There were times we came to blows, so immense\nwas the gulf between our views.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_006: But he just dropped in to tell me he's retiring. To say\ngoodbye.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_007: <NCA>"Why is he retiring?"
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_008: <NCB>"That's a shame."
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_009: <ACA>He doesn't find hope in it anymore. Telling stories,\nthat is. No longer sees the point.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_010: <ACA>I tried to tell him there are still people drawing\ninspiration from his tales of bravery.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_011: <ACB>Truly it is. I told him there are still people drawing\ninspiration from his tales of bravery.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_012: But even as I said it, it felt hollow. We writers,\nwe made generals into heroes, priests into saints...
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_013: and now they're all dead. Oopsy-daisy! So no one\ntrusts us anymore.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_014: Of course, wartime or no, stories are stories.\nFiction is fiction. It's entertainment, not reality.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_015: I just fear that even if the world's body of writers\nsurvives, the heart is dying.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_016: That's why I was so excited for us to face Balor,\nstrange as that may sound.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_017: Not as a warrior, of course, and not out of any\nmisguided desire for knightly honor.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_018: As a writer, I saw a chance to birth a great story.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_019: What could be more inspiring than a climactic battle\nagainst the forces of annihilation and despair?
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_020: It was like a legend forming before my eyes!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_021: I would record the tale of all the heroes battling\ndarkness, even if it meant bothering them slightly.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_022: But Balor, he was more powerful than I imagined.\nHe destroys everything—stories included.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_023: Sorry, I'm not doubting we will be victorious. Merely\nlamenting the powerlessness of my art form.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_024: <NCA>"So, Dante's dead."
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_025: What are you talking about? I'm right here! How else\ncould I be so eloquently— Oh.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_026: You mean to suggest that Dante the writer, her faith\nin the power of stories, no longer exists?
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_027: Well, I'll prove you wrong, Promised One! I'm going\nstraight to my writing desk.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_028: Yes, and after a little research, I'll pen the tale of our\nsaving humanity.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_A_029: The greatest legend in the history of the world,\ncourtesy of Dante, the master auteur!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S: <EDH>
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_001: Oh... How dare you. How dare you! You\nabsolute boob!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_002: You were supposed to have sacrificed yourself in\nthe underworld. You've ruined my ending!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_003: Now I have to rip it all up, my tear-inducing\nmasterpiece, and start over again!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_004: <NCA>"Were you crying?"
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_005: <NCB>"Did you finish writing it?"
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_006: <ACA>Teasing me as I bare my emotions! I see a few days'\ndeath has not changed you.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_007: <ACA>What is it—this strange sensation I'm having?\nNostalgia? Melancholy? Bah, no time for it!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_008: <ACB>Of course. I've done nothing but write! You really\nthought I'd be able to sleep after you disappeared?
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_009: <ACB>I'll spare you the details of my grieving after it\nwas done. There's a more important matter at hand.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_010: I need you to give me an interview—now. We've had\nhardly any chance to talk off the battlefield!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_011: <NCA>"I'm not the savior anymore."
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_012: What does that matter? My protagonist has just\nreturned from the dead!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_013: Someone almost impossibly difficult to get to know.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_014: I've read history back to front, have watched my\nallies' emotions unfold like a spectator at a play.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_015: And yet you remain a confounding mystery!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_016: I need to learn how you became who you are. Now.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_017: Even if it takes me my whole life, I'll scour your\nevery nook and crevice.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_018: The radiant smile that blooms like a flower on\nyour lips, your sky-rending anger... I want it all.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_019: <RSDS>Give it to me, and I'll take it, and never let go!
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_020: The world will have the legend of its salvation,\nas seen through the eyes of the one who saved it.
MID_SE_Ism_Dan_S_021: I'll survive as long as it takes to tell your story—\nwhether you like it or not!